{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And when a man brings a sacrifice of peace-offerings to YHWH.</b> He explains that even though these are lesser holy offerings and do not require maleness, as he explained above in stating ״אִם זָכָר אִם נְקֵבָה״ (Leviticus 3:1), nevertheless they do require wholeness. And he gives the reason for this in stating <b>you shall not offer these to YHWH</b> — for it is not fitting to offer a blemished animal to Elohim, blessed be He. And he adds a second reason in stating <b>and you shall not give any of them as an offering on the altar to YHWH</b> — if perhaps a blemish befell it after the owners had consecrated it, the emurim (portions burned on the altar) are not to go up on the altar, for it is not fitting that there be in the sacrifice a blemish that is repugnant before Him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:19.438274759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}